The Academic Track at FOSS4G 2027 in **Bristol, United Kingdom** is a forum for researchers and practitioners to present original work on free and open source geospatial software, open data and open standards.

Submission to the Academic Track has two mandatory steps: an extended abstract, followed by a full paper for accepted abstracts.

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Timeline</h3>

| Milestone | Date |
| --- | --- |
| Step 1: Abstract submission opens | TBC |
| Step 1: Abstract submission deadline | TBC |
| Abstract review period | TBC |
| Abstract acceptance notification | TBC |
| Step 2: Full paper submission deadline | TBC |
| Conference | 23 to 29 August 2027 |

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Step 1: Abstract submission</h3>

- Abstracts must be written in English.
- Abstracts should be between **800 and 1,000 words**.
- All abstracts are reviewed by the Scientific Committee.

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Step 2: Full paper submission</h3>

Only authors of accepted abstracts are invited to submit a full paper.

- Full papers are limited to **8 pages** and must use the official template, which will be announced with the publication details.
- Papers must present original research that has not been published elsewhere.
- All papers are checked for template conformance and plagiarism.

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Publication</h3>

How and where the FOSS4G 2027 Academic Track proceedings will be published has not been decided yet. Details will be announced here.

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Registration</h3>

All speakers and presenters must <a href="/attend/register">register for the conference</a>.

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Contact</h3>

If you have any questions about the Academic Track, please contact us at [academic@foss4g.org](mailto:academic@foss4g.org).
